# Line endings.
#
# This project is built on Windows and on Linux, and without a rule the two
# disagree about every text file they both touch: a file committed from one
# shows up as a whole-file change on the other. Normalising to LF in the
# repository and leaving the working tree native is the arrangement that
# surprises nobody.
* text=auto

# Formats that must never be line-ending converted, whatever a rule above says.
# A converted PNG or a rewritten WAV is a corrupt file, not a formatting nit.
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.webp     binary
*.ico      binary
*.wav      binary
*.mp3      binary
*.ogg      binary
*.flac     binary
*.so       binary
*.dll      binary
*.dylib    binary
*.exe      binary
*.apk      binary
*.aab      binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks      binary
*.ttf      binary
*.otf      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.blend    binary
*.vhdx     binary

# Generated files that happen to be text. Diffing them tells nobody anything,
# and treating them as text is how merge conflicts get committed.
*.g.dart   linguist-generated=true
pubspec.lock linguist-generated=true

# **Shell scripts are LF in the working tree as well, and this is not a preference.**
#
# `* text=auto` above normalises the repository to LF but leaves the working tree native -- CRLF on Windows.
# That is right for Dart, JSON and Markdown and it is wrong for a script: on 2026-09-23 the Linux build could
# not run from this checkout at all, because bash inside WSL read line 17 as `set -o pipefail` and answered
#
#     tool/build_linux.sh: line 17: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# Every one of the fifteen shell scripts in the repository was CRLF. `eol=lf` pins the working tree copy too,
# so the file that git records and the file Linux executes are the same bytes.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# A Linux build reads this file to learn the version, and a stray CR becomes part of it.
# `packaging/*/build.sh` also strips one defensively; this keeps the file itself clean.
pubspec.yaml text eol=lf
